## Messaging Queue :- 
- Basic concept of the messaging queue is, we have producer and consumer. What is producer and consumer and what are their work? 
- Producer works is to produce message and consumer work is to consume the message. So lets talk about the message. 
- So let a server, which produce the messages frequently and to consume the produced message we have another service lets say, database. In the Notication system we have we have the different notification generated by some service are consumed by the workers/client. 
- So to make the communication between producer and consumer we introduced the queue, and this queue is called messageing queue, where producer apna message dalta rahega and consumer apna message consume karta rahega. and this called the producer and consumer architecture. 

Structure :- 
 - Producer : Produce message
 - Messaging Queue : carray the messages
 - Message Consume : Message consume

### Benifits of Producer/Consumer :- 
- Producer and Consumer can work on their own pace. 

### Synchronous Communication :- 
- Lets say have the MS1 and MS2 which communicate over the Internet through the http call. So in this architecture we are doing the request from MS1 and then MS2 to consume/process it then send the the response the MS1, uske baad wo apna kaam aage kare.
 - During this MS1 have to wait till MS2 process the request from the MS1. So this way communcation is called Synchronous Communication. 

- Structure :- 
 - Microservice1
 - Connection calls
 - Microservice2

### Asynchronous communication :- 
 - So messaging queue help to have the Asynchronous communication. 
 - It says that if the MS1 request to MS2 then MS1 should do their work , without waiting for the response from the MS2. 
 
## Why Messaging Queue
- So we got the idea from the asynchronous, that two services can talk async way. So if   the sceanrio :- 
 - MS1 : A busy service (many request happend here) -> so High Throghput. 
 - MS2 : Nomal Service -> Low Throughput.

- So the MS1 is busy service then so it farword the request to the MS2, basically bombard many request, so is this possible for the MS2 to manage this request. So kya MS2 ka Throghput itna jayda hai ki wo in request ko handle kar sakti hai. 
- If yes then ok If not then MS2 becomes down/crash.


- Throughput : The no. of request that can be managed by any service(microservice). 
- The difinition of the throghput varies from machine learning, computer network, OS, etc But is HLD whenever we talk about the throughput we talk about the OPS (Operations per second). 

Real-wrold Example to understand the Throughput/Messaging Queue :-
The ride plateform like Ola/Uber/Rapido, what this plateform will be doing. So we are having the driver vahicle(Interface), client(user Interface),etc How live Location works?
- Driver vahicle will be giving the GPS signal in every some time to the Ola Server.
- And the Ola server will give this signals to the Client. 
- Structure :- 
  - GPS
  - Ola Server
  - Client

So if we think about the Back of the Envelope Calculations we just don't have one driver and one Client. In just a delhi type of city lets say we have 1 lakhs of driver then we are geting the 1 lakhs request per second on the ola server. Then What data server will be doing with this request :- 
 - Add value to DB -> Reason for computation like calculating the time need to reach the client,etc. 

So if is amount mai data kisi bhi type of Database mai daal raha hoga toh koi bhi database isko handle kar paayega kya. --> No any type database can store this High throughput of data. 
- So if we have the application for the world or cuntry level Lets say on any DB we wil getting very high load. To solve this issue we have the message queues.

### How the message queue like Kafka will be solving the above dicussed issue? 
- Structure :- 
  - GPS : Driver vehicle will share live location. 1 lakh request/sec. 
  - Ola Server
  - Client
  - DB : Server insert request

- Every database that exist will not have such a high throughput. So itna load koi bhi database nahi le sakta hai. 

So we have device which have such very high throughput i.e is Kafka. So now when the Ola server try to put the the request to the Database, now we put the Kafka between the Server and DB. 
 - Now Ola server request the Kafka (kafka server has very high throughput)
 - Now DB will try to consume this request from the kafka server
 - So DB not consume the  request directly from kafka server, so it has worker which will do this work

Flow :- 
 - Ola server works as producer here, becacuse Ola server try to push many request together. 
 - workers are consumers which take the request one by one from the kafka server and and then if some of request are come to the workers then they do Bulk push on the DB. So we can set a timer of the bulk push, ki itne minute baad push karo. 

Note :- We always minimize the hit of the DB. 

DB server :- Its only work is to take a request and give the Database whereas webserver general work is to take the request from client process the request and Put the data in DB. -> Easily scalable then Db server as we can use load-balancer,etc

## Kafka
Why it is Useful?
 - Pace matching : We have discussed above that agar ek service request fast send kar raha hai aur ek service slow hai, means utna fast request handle nahi kar sakta then we can use Kafka. -> related to storing
 - Async Communication : So When a service request service and expect response so it can do its work, here to we can use we can send our request to kafka and from their consumer take the request and process the request, notify or generate the event to tell the service that processes data is ready. 
 
### Indepth Architecture of Kafka
Terms we will use :- 
1. Cluster
2. Broker 
3. Topic
4. Partition
5. Offset
6. Zookeeper
7. Consumer
8. Consumer Group
9. Producer

- The basic architecture we will bw having. We have a producer and consumer. So producer and consumer want to interact with each other, it can directly interact with each other so if do this they become synchronized, if they are Asynchronous then there may be the problem of pace matching. 
- So the soulution of this messaging queue, we introduced the messaging queue, which is kafka server/ Broker. -> Kafka will be also deploy at any server and that server is called Broker. 
- Different topics exist in kafka is :- 
  1. Topic 0 
  2. Topic 1

  - Topic : Assume the Topic as a whatsapp group such as we have friends group, family group, class group, trip group, study group,etc. Kafka says that you will be sending different type of messages on it. Like we discussed about Ola so there may rider location, notifications, etc different type of message ko usne topic mai divide kar diya. 

- In the Topic we have partitions. Partition indexing will be exist there, starting with 0. Partition are actual queue, where the message are stored. So the producer put the message in the partition. 
- In Partition we have offsets. Offset are just like the small box or index of an array. Where we store the message.
- The message m will be stored in the offset of thr partition. starting with 0 index. 

### Introducing Producer-consumer Interactions :- 
- So firstly the producer will push the message in the any of the topic to any of partition of any offset. How we selecting the topic we will see later. 
- Lets say :- 
   topic 0 --> Rider location related message
   topic 1 --> notifications 
- Lets say m1 and m2 are stored the topic 0. So consumer will firstly the consume the message m1. 

### Consumer Groups and How consumer actually consumes messages. 
Structure :- 
 - Producer
 - Broker : topic0 -> patition(0,1,2,3) -> Offset(0,1,2,3)
 - Consumer Group : Consumer1 , Consumer2 

- No consumer can exist without a consumer group. In the consumer group we have only one consumer for now. 
- Producer will push the message in the partition. And consumer wants to read this partition, then for this kafka server do Auto-Balancing. So if we have one partion and one consumer only then kafka server we make sure that consumer will able to listen that partition. 
 - So if we have one more partition then the auto balancing will make sure that cosumer1 will listen both partotion we have. Similarly if one more partition then consume1 will listen that too. 

- If we intoduced one more consumer lets say consumer2 then what happend now which consumer will listen which partition? -> So usme kuchh partion ko consumer1 and kuchh ko consumer 2 listen karega. If the partition are even then equall no of partition will given to both two consumer we have. 
- If have one more(odd) partition then any one can listen the last partition we introduced. 

- So Auto balancing try to distribute the partition into evenly so no consumer have any type of load. 

- If we have only one partition and have two consumer then what will be happen? So its allocate to any one consumer, jo pahle se hoga/aayega usko milega. Lets suppose consumer1 pahle aaya tha aur wo partition ko sun raha tha, Now if consumer2 come and ask to Broker about the partition if have then consumer is ready to listen.
 - Broker will never allocate two consumer to same partition 

Note :- If number of partition are less then number of consumers, some consumers will remain idle. So 1 consumer can consume many partition but 1 partition can be consumed by only one consumer. 

### More than one consumer group
Structure :- 
 - Producer
 - Broker : topic0 -> patition(0,) -> Offset(0,1,2,3)
 - Consumer Group1 : Consumer1 , Consumer2
 - Consumer Group2: Consumer1 , Consumer2

- Now after introducing new consumer group we are trying to do Auto- Balancing. Both consumer group have the two-two consumer now. 
- So if has one partition in the broker then it simply assign any of the consumer of consumer group1 and consumer group2.
 -> So ek partition ko ek he consumer sun sakta hai from consumer group. So different consumer can listen the same partition in the same different consumer group. 
- If one more partition then it will assign two the both groups -> jo idle hai abhi. 

Note:- Jaise hamane abhi dekha tha ki kaise ek group mai Auto balancing kaam kar raha tha waise karega laki ab dono group mai karega. -> Many of the Interview problem's cpme through this concept. 

Why Kafka does all this? Why consumer grups? why not same partition ko same gruop ke two consumer can listen? Why not we take just queue and we put request there and consumer take it from there?
- Consumer Group concept is fairly new in kafka.
- Messaging queues serve 2 purpose : 
  1. Queue (FIFO) : act like queue we have studied
  2. act like pub/sub model

### First Model: Consumer-Producer
- Earlier the concept of the messaging queue is like  we will have the producer, queue and consumer, in this concept produceris responsible normally push the operations and consumer pull the operation. So in this we will have the one producer and one consumer corresponding.

### Second Model : Pub/sub 
- After this we got the pub/sub Model (Publisher/subscriber model), this model says that we have publisher at the place of producer, queue( Broadcasting type of queue) and subscriber(at the place consumer). We may have the multiple subscriber can listen the queue. In this we have 1 producer and many consumer.
 - Real world example: Lets suppose you have youtube chennal and upload a video and you want that the notifications of new should go to all user who followed you. 

- kafka is invent by the LinkedIn. So we have gone through all the two model we have discussed above,  so Kafka has implemented the first purpose of the messaging queue using only one consumer group it is applicable earlier.
 - So kafka want to integrate the pub-sub model, so we cannot do when we have single consumer group because we donot allow multiple conumer to listen single partition. So introduced consumer group concept. Using the Consumer group concept it works as pub-sub model and using only one consumer group kafka work as normal producer-consumer ke tarh kaam karta hai. 

### Zookeper :- 
Structure :- 
 - Producer
 - Broker : topic0 -> patition(0) -> Offset(0,1,2,3)
 - Consumer Group1 : Consumer1 , Consumer2 
 - Zookeeper 

 Zookeeper: Zookeeper is a service and it is exist indepenendantly beofore the kafka. Kafka just use the zookeeper for some purpose. 
 - Lets say we have one partition and one group having two consumer i.e consumer1 and consumer2. Consumer1 one is listening the partion and consumer2 remain ideal. Zookeeper store all this information in it. 
  like:-
      Consumer group:1
      Consumer : 1
      Topic : 0
      Partition : 0 
      Offset : 0 
    
  - All the info of the messaging queue hierarchy is liestening is stored here which topic, which gropup, which partition and which offset,etc jo currently is being listened is stored hare. 
  - It store the information because if the any of the consumer go down then other consumer if exist that will listen it will be done by the broker itself. So how the new assigned consumer will know that from it has to start reading the operation. For this we have the zookeeper. 
  - The work of zookeeper is only this in kafka, we will be learning more about the zookeeper in future. 

### Clusters:-